s($,"b1T","jH",()=>{var q="India",p="Social Activist",o="Uttar Pradesh, India",n="Rajasthan, India",m="Madhya Pradesh, India",l="Social Entrepreneur",k="Tamil Nadu, India",j="Maharashtra, India",i="Delhi, India",h="Human Rights Activist",g="Karnataka, India",f="Foreign",e="New York, USA",d="Philanthropist"
return A.a([A.bD(q,A.bB().ba(B.IS),"Jadav Payeng","1","Created a 1,360-acre forest single-handedly. Provided habitat for endangered species including tigers and rhinos. Inspired millions worldwide to take environmental action.",!0,3421,"Assam, India","Environmental Activist","Jadav Payeng single-handedly planted a 1,360-acre forest on a barren sandbar in Assam over 40 years. Starting at age 16 in 1979, he planted bamboo and trees every day. What was once a wasteland is now a thriving forest, home to Bengal tigers, Indian rhinoceros, over 100 deer, and countless birds. He continues to plant trees daily, dedicating his life to nature.","The Man Who Planted a Forest"),A.bD(q,A.bB().ba(B.J0),"Dr. Tessy Thomas","2","First woman to lead India's ballistic missile program. Successfully developed Agni-IV and Agni-V missiles. Inspired thousands of women to enter STEM fields.",!0,2847,"Kerala, India","Aerospace Scientist","Dr. Tessy Thomas became the first woman scientist to head a missile project in India. She led the Agni-IV and Agni-V missile projects, earning the title 'Missile Woman of India'. Despite facing gender discrimination in a male-dominated field, she broke barriers and became the Director General of Aeronautical Systems, inspiring countless young women to pursue careers in science and technology.","India's Missile Woman"),A.bD(q,A.bB().ba(B.J7),"Sampat Pal Devi","3","Founded Gulabi Gang with 400,000+ members. Prevented hundreds of child marriages. Rescued countless women from domestic violence.",!1,2156,o,p,"Married at age 12 and facing domestic violence, Sampat Pal Devi founded the 'Gulabi Gang' (Pink Gang) - a group of women vigilantes dressed in pink saris who fight against domestic abuse, child marriage, and corruption. With over 400,000 members, they patrol villages, confront abusive husbands, and even take on corrupt officials. They've prevented countless child marriages and saved women from violence.","The Bandit Queen Turned Social Reformer"),A.bD(q,A.bB().ba(B.Ib),"Rajendra Singh","4","Revived 5 rivers in Rajasthan. Brought water to 1,000+ villages. Won Stockholm Water Prize in 2015.",!0,1876,n,"Water Conservationist","Rajendra Singh revived five rivers in Rajasthan that had been dry for decades. Using traditional water conservation techniques, he built johads (rainwater storage tanks) and convinced villagers to change their water usage habits. His work brought water back to over 1,000 villages and revived the Arvari River. He won the Stockholm Water Prize and is called the 'Waterman of India'.","The Waterman of India"),A.bD(q,A.bB().ba(B.Ii),"Kailash Satyarthi","5","Rescued 90,000+ children from slavery and trafficking. Won Nobel Peace Prize in 2014. Changed global child labor laws.",!0,4521,m,"Child Rights Activist","Kailash Satyarthi has rescued over 90,000 children from slavery, human trafficking, and child labor through his organization Bachpan Bachao Andolan. He risked his life countless times, facing violent opposition from traffickers. His advocacy led to international conventions on child rights. In 2014, he won the Nobel Peace Prize for his tireless work to end child exploitation.","From Child Laborer to Education Champion"),A.bD(q,A.bB().ba(B.Iv),"Dashrath Manjhi","6","Carved a road through a mountain alone in 22 years. Reduced village-to-town distance from 55km to 15km. Saved countless lives by providing medical access.",!0,3987,"Bihar, India","Laborer","When his wife died because they couldn't reach the hospital in time due to a mountain blocking the path, Dashrath Manjhi spent 22 years single-handedly carving a 360-foot-long, 30-feet-wide road through the mountain using only a hammer and chisel. He reduced the distance between his village and the nearest town from 55 km to 15 km, providing access to medical care, schools, and jobs for thousands.","The Mountain Man"),A.bD(q,A.bB().ba(B.J3),"Harshini Kanhekar","7","First female firefighter in India. Saved dozens of lives. Inspired women nationwide to join emergency services.",!1,1654,m,"Firefighter","At 25, Harshini Kanhekar became India's first female firefighter, breaking into an exclusively male profession. She faced discrimination and skepticism but proved herself through rigorous training and dedication. She has saved numerous lives, fought major fires, and inspired hundreds of women to join emergency services across India.","India's First Female Firefighter"),A.bD(q,A.bB().ba(B.Ip),"Arunachalam Muruganantham","8","Invented low-cost sanitary pad machine. Empowered 1000+ women entrepreneurs. Featured in TIME's 100 Most Influential People.",!0,2943,k,l,"When Muruganantham discovered his wife using rags during menstruation due to the high cost of sanitary pads, he spent years developing a low-cost sanitary pad making machine. He faced ridicule, was called crazy, and even his wife left him. But he persisted, eventually creating machines that rural women could use to make and sell affordable pads, transforming menstrual hygiene across India.","The Pad Man"),A.bD(q,A.bB().ba(B.Iy),"Bunker Roy","9","Trained women from 96 countries as solar engineers. Brought electricity to 1000+ villages. Empowered thousands of rural women.",!1,1432,n,"Social Activist & Educator","Bunker Roy founded the Barefoot College, which trains illiterate and semi-literate rural women to become solar engineers, water drillers, and architects. These 'barefoot' professionals then bring modern amenities to their villages. The college has trained women from 96 countries, bringing solar electricity to over 1,000 villages and impacting millions of lives.","The Barefoot College Founder"),A.bD(q,A.bB().ba(B.J8),"Dr. Prakash Baba Amte","10","Treated 300,000+ patients for free in tribal areas. Built hospitals and schools in remote regions. Rescued countless injured wild animals.",!1,2103,j,"Doctor & Social Worker","Dr. Prakash Amte gave up a comfortable city life to serve tribal communities and wildlife in Maharashtra's forests. Despite Naxalite threats, he built hospitals and schools in remote areas, treating over 300,000 patients for free. He also runs an animal orphanage, caring for injured wildlife. He's been stabbed, threatened, but never gave up on his mission.","The Miracle Doctor of Mumbai"),A.bD(q,A.bB().ba(B.Jb),"Rajesh Kumar Sharma","11","Taught 300+ underprivileged children for free. Many students now attend formal schools. Inspired similar initiatives across India.",!1,1765,i,"Teacher","For over 8 years, Rajesh has been teaching slum children under a metro bridge in Delhi. He noticed poor children had no access to education, so he started teaching them for free with just a blackboard. Despite having a low income himself, he spends his own money on books and supplies. He's educated over 300 children, many of whom have gone on to attend regular schools.","The School Under the Bridge"),A.bD(q,A.bB().ba(B.Ie),"Dr. K.S. Gopi Sundar","12","Saved the Sarus Crane from near extinction. Protected 1000+ crane nests. Pioneered community-based wildlife conservation.",!1,987,o,"Wildlife Biologist","Dr. Gopi Sundar has dedicated his life to saving the critically endangered Sarus Crane. He works with farmers to protect crane nests in agricultural fields, compensating them for crop damage. His innovative community-based conservation approach has increased crane populations and changed how India approaches wildlife conservation in human-dominated landscapes.","India's Crane Man"),A.bD(q,A.bB().ba(B.J5),"Swati Bedekar","13","Employed 100+ acid attack survivors and underprivileged women. Distributed millions of eco-friendly sanitary pads. Provided dignity and income to marginalized women.",!1,1543,j,l,"Swati founded an organization that employs acid attack survivors and underprivileged women to manufacture eco-friendly, biodegradable sanitary napkins. She provides them with employment, dignity, and financial independence while solving the menstrual hygiene problem. Her initiative has employed over 100 women and distributed millions of affordable pads.","The Sanitary Napkin Revolutionary"),A.bD(q,A.bB().ba(B.J1),"Sathya Sankaran","14","Taught 5000+ women to cycle. Promoted eco-friendly transportation. Broke social barriers for women's mobility.",!1,1234,k,"Cycling Advocate","Sathya became India's first 'Bicycle Mayor', promoting cycling as eco-friendly transportation in Chennai. She organizes women's cycling groups, teaches cycling to those who never learned, and advocates for cycling infrastructure. She's empowered thousands of women to cycle independently, breaking social taboos and reducing pollution.","The Bicycle Mayor"),A.bD(q,A.bB().ba(B.Ih),"Karimul Hak","15","Transported 5,500+ patients for free on bike ambulance. Saved hundreds of lives in remote areas. Recognized with Padma Shri award.",!0,2876,"West Bengal, India","Ambulance Driver","Karimul, a tea garden worker earning minimal wages, bought a motorcycle and converted it into a 'bike ambulance' to transport sick people from remote villages to hospitals. He has transported over 5,500 patients for free, often using his own money for fuel. He works day and night, never refusing anyone, saving countless lives in areas with no road access.","The Ambulance Driver Who Never Says No"),A.bD(q,A.bB().ba(B.In),"Bezwada Wilson","16","Liberated 300,000+ manual scavengers. Won Ramon Magsaysay Award. Led to ban on manual scavenging in India.",!0,2234,g,h,"Bezwada Wilson has fought for 35 years to end manual scavenging - the inhumane practice of manually cleaning sewers and toilets. Born into a manual scavenging family, he founded the Safai Karmachari Andolan, liberating over 300,000 manual scavengers and providing them alternative livelihoods. He won the Ramon Magsaysay Award for his fearless advocacy.","The Sewer Diving Savior"),A.bD(q,A.bB().ba(B.Iz),"Irom Sharmila","17","Held 16-year hunger strike for human rights. Brought international attention to Northeast India issues. Inspired thousands of activists.",!0,3156,"Manipur, India","Civil Rights Activist","Irom Sharmila held the world's longest hunger strike - 16 years - demanding the repeal of the Armed Forces Special Powers Act after witnessing a massacre. She was force-fed through tubes in detention but never gave up. Though her fast ended, her sacrifice brought global attention to human rights issues in Northeast India and inspired a generation of activists.","The Iron Lady of Manipur"),A.bD(q,A.bB().ba(B.Ja),"Subhash Palekar","18","Developed Zero Budget Natural Farming. Adopted by 4 million+ farmers. Saved farmers from debt and suicide.",!1,1687,j,"Agricultural Scientist","Subhash Palekar developed Zero Budget Natural Farming (ZBNF), a method that eliminates the need for expensive fertilizers and pesticides. After seeing farmers commit suicide due to debt, he spent years researching and promoting natural farming. His methods have been adopted by over 4 million farmers across India, freeing them from debt and chemical dependency.","The Organic Farming Pioneer"),A.bD(q,A.bB().ba(B.Ic),"Laxmi Agarwal","19","Led campaign for stricter acid sale regulations. Supreme Court ruled in favor due to her petition. Helped 100+ acid attack survivors rebuild lives.",!0,2765,i,"Activist","Laxmi was 15 when she was attacked with acid by a man whose advances she rejected. Instead of hiding, she became a leading campaigner for acid attack survivors' rights. She fought for stricter laws on acid sales, won landmark legal victories, and founded an organization helping survivors. Her courage has changed laws and inspired countless survivors to speak up.","The Acid Attack Fighter"),A.bD(q,A.bB().ba(B.It),"Medha Patkar","20","Advocated for 100,000+ displaced families. Fought for fair rehabilitation policies. Challenged unjust development projects nationwide.",!1,1543,j,p,"Medha Patkar has spent over 30 years fighting for the rights of people displaced by big dams and development projects. Through the Narmada Bachao Andolan, she's fought against unfair displacement, often facing violence and arrest. She's advocated for rehabilitation and fair compensation for thousands of displaced families, challenging powerful corporations and governments.","The Garbage Warrior"),A.bD(q,A.bB().ba(B.Ik),"Javed Abidi","21","Led to Rights of Persons with Disabilities Act 2016. Made thousands of public spaces accessible. Gave voice to 70 million disabled Indians.",!1,1876,i,"Disability Rights Activist","Born with spina bifida and using a wheelchair, Javed Abidi became India's most prominent disability rights advocate. He fought for accessibility laws, making public spaces wheelchair-friendly, and ensuring disabled people got equal opportunities. His advocacy led to the Rights of Persons with Disabilities Act 2016, transforming lives of millions of disabled Indians.","The Voice of Disability Rights"),A.bD(q,A.bB().ba(B.J4),"Murli Manohar","22","Rescued 30,000+ snakes from urban areas. Prevented thousands of snake killings. Educated communities about snake conservation.",!1,1324,g,"Wildlife Rescuer","Murli has rescued over 30,000 snakes from urban areas and released them into the wild. Available 24/7, he responds to distress calls, educates people about snakes, and has prevented countless snake killings. Despite being bitten multiple times, he continues his mission, changing people's perception of snakes and preventing human-wildlife conflict.","The Snake Rescuer"),A.bD(q,A.bB().ba(B.Ig),"Sant Balbir Singh Seechewal","23","Revived 160-km polluted river to clean flowing state. Inspired community-led river cleaning across Punjab. Restored ecological balance.",!1,1567,"Punjab, India","Environmentalist","Sant Seechewal revived the 160-km long Kali Bein river, a tributary of Sutlej, which had turned into a sewage drain. With community support, he cleaned tons of garbage, stopped sewage flow, and restored the river's sanctity. The river now flows clean, attracting migratory birds and serving thousands of villagers. He's now working on cleaning other rivers.","The River Doctor"),A.bD(q,A.bB().ba(B.J9),"Usha Muruganantham","24","Trained 2,000+ women entrepreneurs. Brought affordable menstrual hygiene to millions. Broke menstrual taboos in rural India.",!1,1432,k,l,"After her husband's invention of low-cost sanitary pads, Usha became a key figure in spreading menstrual hygiene awareness. She trains rural women to operate pad-making machines, creating employment and breaking menstrual taboos. She's empowered over 2,000 women entrepreneurs and brought menstrual hygiene to millions of rural women who couldn't afford commercial pads.","The Menstrual Man's Wife"),A.bD(q,A.bB().ba(B.J2),"Rakesh Shukla","25","Feeds 500+ street dogs daily. Rescued and treated 3,000+ dogs. Promoted adoption and humane treatment of strays.",!1,1198,o,"Animal Welfare Activist","Rakesh founded Voice of Stray Dogs, feeding over 500 street dogs daily in Noida. With his own money and donations, he's vaccinated thousands of dogs, provided medical care, and found homes for hundreds. He works tirelessly to change perceptions about street dogs, promoting adoption and humane treatment. His shelter has saved over 3,000 dogs from death.","The Stray Dog Angel"),A.bD(f,A.bB().ba(B.IJ),"Sadio Man\xe9","26","Built hospital and school in home village. Provides monthly stipends to 70+ families. Funded infrastructure worth over \u20ac1 million in Senegal.",!0,5432,"Bambali, Senegal","Professional Footballer","Despite earning millions as a top footballer, Sadio Man\xe9 lives humbly and donates most of his wealth to his home village in Senegal. He built a school, hospital, post office, and provides monthly stipends to families. He personally funded a \u20ac700,000 hospital and \u20ac250,000 school. When asked why he doesn't own luxury items, he said: 'Why would I want 10 Ferraris? I want my people to have access to healthcare and education.'","The Footballer Who Builds Schools"),A.bD(f,A.bB().ba(B.IC),"Nicholas Winton","27","Saved 669 children from Holocaust. Organized 8 trainloads of child refugees. Over 6,000 descendants alive today because of him.",!0,4876,"London, United Kingdom","Humanitarian","In 1939, Nicholas Winton organized the rescue of 669 children, mostly Jewish, from Czechoslovakia before the Nazi invasion. He arranged their transport to Britain and found foster homes for them. He kept this secret for 50 years until his wife discovered a scrapbook. In 1988, he was reunited with the children (now adults) he saved on live television in an emotional moment that shocked the world.","The Man Who Saved 669 Children"),A.bD(f,A.bB().ba(B.IG),"Malala Yousafzai","28","Youngest Nobel Prize winner at 17. Malala Fund supported education for thousands of girls. Opened schools in Lebanon, Turkey, and Pakistan.",!0,6234,"Swat Valley, Pakistan","Education Activist","At 11, Malala began blogging about girls' education under Taliban rule. At 15, she was shot in the head by Taliban gunmen for advocating education. She survived and became a global advocate for girls' education. At 17, she became the youngest Nobel Prize laureate. She's opened schools, advocated globally, and her fund has supported education for girls in over 8 countries.","The Pakistani Girl Who Defied Taliban"),A.bD(f,A.bB().ba(B.IK),"Oskar Schindler","29","Saved 1,200 Jews from Holocaust. Spent entire fortune protecting them. Over 8,500 descendants alive today.",!0,5123,"Krak\xf3w, Poland","Industrialist","German industrialist Oskar Schindler saved 1,200 Jews during the Holocaust by employing them in his factories, claiming they were essential workers. He spent his entire fortune bribing Nazi officials to protect them. He died penniless but is honored as 'Righteous Among the Nations'. His story inspired the film 'Schindler's List', bringing his heroism to millions.","The List That Saved Lives"),A.bD(f,A.bB().ba(B.Iq),"Wesley Autrey","30","Saved a stranger's life by jumping in front of oncoming subway train. Inspired worldwide acts of courage. Met President Bush and received numerous awards.",!1,3456,e,"Construction Worker","Wesley Autrey jumped onto subway tracks to save a stranger who had fallen and was having a seizure, with a train approaching. He held the man down in the drainage trench as the train passed inches above them. Both survived. When asked why he risked his life, he simply said, 'I don't feel like I did something spectacular; I just saw someone who needed help.'","The Subway Hero"),A.bD(f,A.bB().ba(B.IM),"Dr. Jerry Brown","31","Treated 2,000+ Ebola patients. Survived Ebola and returned to work. Inspired medical workers to continue fighting the outbreak.",!0,2987,"Liberia","Doctor","Dr. Jerry Brown stayed in Liberia during the 2014 Ebola outbreak when many healthcare workers fled. He treated thousands of patients despite the extreme risk, working 18-hour days in full protective gear. He contracted Ebola himself but survived and returned to treating patients. His courage saved countless lives and inspired other medical workers to stay and fight.","The Doctor Who Fought Ebola"),A.bD(f,A.bB().ba(B.Ij),"Antonio Vicente","32","Planted 40,000+ trees over 40 years. Restored forest ecosystem. Brought back endangered wildlife to the region.",!1,2345,"Brazil","Farmer","After seeing his region's forests destroyed, Brazilian farmer Antonio Vicente spent 40 years planting over 40,000 trees by hand on his property. What was once barren land is now a lush forest with returning wildlife including jaguars and pumas. He continues planting, saying 'The forest is life. Without it, we have nothing.'","The Man Who Planted 40,000 Trees"),A.bD(f,A.bB().ba(B.Jc),"Elmer Alvarez","33","Returned $17,000 despite being homeless. Inspired $140,000 in donations. Now helps other homeless veterans.",!1,2876,"Connecticut, USA","Homeless Veteran","Homeless Iraq War veteran Elmer Alvarez found a check for $10,000 and $7,000 in cash outside a bank. Despite being homeless and struggling, he immediately returned it to the bank. His honesty touched the nation, and a fundraiser raised over $140,000 for him. He used the money to get housing and now helps other homeless veterans.","The Homeless Man Who Returned $17,000"),A.bD(f,A.bB().ba(B.IB),"Sister Rosemary Nyirumbe","34","Rehabilitated 2,000+ girls who escaped LRA captivity. Provided education and counseling. Continues despite death threats.",!0,2543,"Uganda","Nun & Director","Sister Rosemary runs a safe haven in Uganda for girls who escaped Joseph Kony's Lord's Resistance Army. Many were forced to be child soldiers and sex slaves. She provides them education, counseling, and vocational training. She's rehabilitated over 2,000 girls, helping them heal and rebuild their lives. She faces death threats but continues her mission.","The Nurse Who Never Stopped"),A.bD(f,A.bB().ba(B.IQ),"Dr. Li Wenliang","35","First to warn about COVID-19. Alerted medical community despite government suppression. Honored as a hero after his death.",!0,7654,"Wuhan, China","Ophthalmologist","Dr. Li Wenliang was among the first to warn about the COVID-19 outbreak in December 2019. He was reprimanded by authorities and forced to sign a letter saying he spread false rumors. He continued treating patients and contracted COVID-19 himself, dying at age 34. His early warning, though suppressed, alerted medical professionals and potentially saved millions of lives.","The Whistleblower Who Saved Lives"),A.bD(f,A.bB().ba(B.IF),"Ranjitsinh Disale","36","Won $1 million Global Teacher Prize. Donated $500,000 to other teachers. His QR code textbook innovation used globally.",!0,3234,"Maharashtra, India (Living in UK)","Teacher","Although Indian, Ranjitsinh works internationally after winning the Global Teacher Prize. He transformed a dilapidated school with no girls enrolled into a model school. He translated textbooks into his students' native language using QR codes, pioneered innovative teaching methods, and now his techniques are used globally. He donated half his $1 million prize money to fellow teachers.","The Teacher Who Walked Miles"),A.bD(f,A.bB().ba(B.IT),"Rick Rescorla","37","Saved 2,700 lives on 9/11. Predicted attack and prepared evacuation plans. Died a hero searching for survivors.",!0,8234,e,"Security Chief","On 9/11, Rick Rescorla saved 2,700 lives by evacuating Morgan Stanley employees from the World Trade Center. He predicted a terrorist attack years earlier and conducted regular evacuation drills. When the towers were hit, he calmly directed evacuations, singing to calm people down. He went back to check for stragglers and died when the building collapsed.","The Firefighter Who Ran Into Hell"),A.bD(f,A.bB().ba(B.IW),"Chiune Sugihara","38","Saved 6,000+ Jews by issuing visas against orders. Sacrificed career for humanity. Over 40,000 descendants alive today.",!0,4532,"Lithuania","Diplomat","Japanese diplomat Chiune Sugihara issued thousands of transit visas to Jewish refugees in 1940, defying his government's orders. He wrote visas by hand for 18-20 hours a day, even throwing visas from the train as he was forced to leave. He saved an estimated 6,000 Jews. He was fired and lived in obscurity until Israel honored him in 1985.","The Japanese Schindler"),A.bD(f,A.bB().ba(B.IP),"Abdul Sattar Edhi","39","Built 1,800-ambulance network. Established orphanages and hospitals nationwide. Rescued 20,000+ abandoned babies personally.",!0,5432,"Karachi, Pakistan",d,"Abdul Sattar Edhi started with a single ambulance and built Pakistan's largest welfare organization. He lived in a tiny apartment above his clinic, wore the same clothes for years, and ate simple food while his foundation ran 1,800 ambulances, orphanages, shelters, and hospitals. He personally cared for abandoned babies and dying patients. He saved thousands of lives.","The Taxi Driver Who Fed Thousands"),A.bD(f,A.bB().ba(B.IX),"Irena Sendler","40","Saved 2,500 Jewish children from Holocaust. Tortured but never revealed names. Over 6,000 descendants alive today.",!0,6123,"Warsaw, Poland","Social Worker","Irena Sendler smuggled 2,500 Jewish children out of the Warsaw Ghetto during the Holocaust, providing them false identities and hiding them with Polish families. She kept records of their real names buried in jars, hoping to reunite them with families after the war. She was caught, tortured by the Gestapo, and sentenced to death, but was rescued. She never considered herself a hero.","The Woman Who Hid 2,500 Children"),A.bD(f,A.bB().ba(B.II),"Arn Chorn-Pond","41","Cleared 1,000+ landmines. Built schools for 10,000+ children. Preserved Cambodian traditional music and arts.",!1,2345,"Cambodia",h,"Arn survived the Cambodian genocide as a child soldier. He escaped to America but returned to Cambodia to help landmine victims and preserve Khmer culture. He founded organizations that cleared landmines, built schools, and trained musicians to preserve traditional arts nearly wiped out by the Khmer Rouge. He's saved countless lives from landmines and preserved Cambodia's cultural heritage.","The Bike Mechanic Who Saved Refugees"),A.bD(f,A.bB().ba(B.IN),"James Harrison","42","Donated blood 1,173 times over 60 years. Saved 2.4 million babies with rare antibodies. Most generous blood donor in history.",!0,4567,"Sydney, Australia","Blood Donor","James Harrison donated blood every week for 60 years - over 1,000 donations. His blood contained rare antibodies that prevent Rhesus disease in newborns. His donations saved an estimated 2.4 million babies, including his own grandson. Despite being terrified of needles, he continued donating until he was 81. He's called 'The Man with the Golden Arm.'","The Janitor Who Became a Hero"),A.bD(f,A.bB().ba(B.Io),"Jos\xe9 Andr\xe9s","43","Served over 100 million meals in disaster zones. Active in 400+ disaster responses. Provides food with dignity globally.",!0,3876,"Washington D.C., USA","Chef & Humanitarian","Chef Jos\xe9 Andr\xe9s founded World Central Kitchen, serving millions of meals in disaster zones. After Hurricane Maria in Puerto Rico, he served 3.7 million meals. He's been to Haiti, Bahamas, California wildfires, and Ukraine war zones. He uses his culinary skills to provide dignity through food, often arriving before official aid. He's fed millions worldwide.","The Professor Who Fed the Hungry"),A.bD(f,A.bB().ba(B.IE),"Bill Gates (Post-Microsoft)","44","Donated $50+ billion to global health. Eradicated polio in multiple countries. Saved millions of lives through vaccine programs.",!0,5234,"Seattle, USA",d,"After leaving Microsoft, Bill Gates dedicated his life to philanthropy. Through the Gates Foundation, he's fought malaria, polio, and diseases affecting the world's poorest. He's donated over $50 billion, funded vaccine research, improved sanitation, and pledged to give away 95% of his wealth. His work has saved millions of lives in Africa and Asia.","The Banker Who Lives Like a Monk"),A.bD(f,A.bB().ba(B.Id),"Boyan Slat","45","Removed 10+ million kg of plastic from oceans. Cleaned Great Pacific Garbage Patch. Youngest recipient of UN's Champions of the Earth award.",!0,4123,"Netherlands","Inventor & Environmentalist","At 16, Boyan Slat founded The Ocean Cleanup after seeing more plastic than fish while diving in Greece. He developed systems to remove plastic from oceans using natural currents. His invention has removed millions of kilograms of plastic from the Great Pacific Garbage Patch. He's now 29 and has cleaned multiple ocean gyres worldwide.","The Surfer Who Cleans Oceans"),A.bD(f,A.bB().ba(B.J6),"Morrie Boogart","46","Knitted 8,000+ hats for children with cancer. Brought joy to thousands of sick children. Continues despite arthritis at age 99.",!1,2134,"Michigan, USA","Retiree","At 87, Morrie Boogart knits 6-8 hats per week for children with cancer at a local hospital. She's made over 8,000 hats in 12 years, each one with love and vibrant colors to cheer up sick children. Despite arthritis in her hands, she continues knitting, saying 'If I can bring a smile to one child's face, it's all worth it.'","The Grandma Who Knit 600 Hats"),A.bD(f,A.bB().ba(B.IR),"Chesley 'Sully' Sullenberger","47","Saved 155 lives through emergency Hudson River landing. Remained calm under extreme pressure. Became symbol of professionalism and heroism.",!0,6543,e,"Airline Pilot","When both engines failed on US Airways Flight 1549, Captain Sully made an emergency landing on the Hudson River, saving all 155 passengers and crew. With only 208 seconds to make a decision, he remained calm, calculated, and executed a perfect water landing. He was the last to leave the plane, walking the aisle twice to ensure everyone was safe.","The Pilot Who Landed on the Hudson"),A.bD(f,A.bB().ba(B.IV),"Alia Muhammad Baker","48","Saved 30,000 books and manuscripts from destruction. Preserved 700-year-old historical documents. Risked life to protect cultural heritage.",!1,2876,"Basra, Iraq","Librarian","When war came to Iraq in 2003, librarian Alia Muhammad Baker saved 30,000 books from Basra's Central Library before it burned down. Despite government refusal to help, she and friends smuggled books to safety over 9 days. She suffered severe burns trying to save more. The books, some 700 years old, survived thanks to her bravery.","The Librarian Who Saved Books"),A.bD(f,A.bB().ba(B.IL),"Xu Chao","49","Donated life savings of $15,000 despite being homeless. Saved 5 lives through organ donation. Inspired organ donation movement in China.",!1,3234,"Ningbo, China","Beggar","Xu Chao was a beggar who saved every penny for 17 years. When diagnosed with terminal brain cancer, he donated all his savings ($15,000) and registered as an organ donor. He said 'I never did anything meaningful in life. At least my organs can help others.' His organs saved 5 lives, and his story inspired thousands to become donors.","The Beggar Who Donated His Organs"),A.bD(f,A.bB().ba(B.Iu),"Jos\xe9 Alberto Guti\xe9rrez","50","Rescued 25,000 books from garbage. Created free community library. Helped thousands of underprivileged children learn to read.",!0,2987,"Bogot\xe1, Colombia","Garbage Collector","For 20 years, Jos\xe9 rescued books from garbage trucks in Bogot\xe1. He collected over 25,000 books and opened a community library in his home, providing free books to poor children. His library has helped thousands of children develop a love for reading. He says, 'I may be a garbage collector to some, but I am a guardian of books to children.'","The Garbage Collector Who Found Hope")],A.aK("I<iZ>"))})
